Fix: "KV LOAD"/"KV STORE" lines (v1/kv_offload/transfer_log.py, wired
from distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/offloading/scheduler.py)
hard to interpret, e.g.:

    KV STORE chatcmpl-... | VRAM -> RAM  |   4 blk /  53248 tok

Reported directly by the user as confusing: "which blocks were
transferred" isn't answerable from this line, and "53248 tok" reads like
the size of a 4-block transfer when it isn't one.

Root cause (STORE side): the token column was `num_offloadable_tokens`
-- `_calc_num_offloadable_tokens()`'s result, essentially the request's
whole computed-so-far frontier (~= req.num_computed_tokens), not the
span this specific store moved. keys_to_store also spans every KV group
(3 mamba + 1 full-attention in this deployment) with potentially
different per-group progress, so there was never a single well-defined
"tokens in this transfer" number available at the old call site --
that's why the existing code comment already warned "not meant to
divide into each other" rather than trying to fix it. Also, "VRAM ->
RAM" reads like an eviction (blocks leaving VRAM) when a store is
actually a COPY: the source blocks stay resident in VRAM (they have to,
to be storable at all) and only gain a backup on the RAM tier.

Fix:
- STORE: derive the actual per-round delta from each group's
  `next_stored_chunk_idx` (the same counter `_build_store_jobs`'s loop
  already advances) -- take the MIN across groups both before and after
  this round's advance (the same "shortest group wins" reasoning the
  HIT_DIVERGED rescue elsewhere in this codebase uses for exactly this
  kind of per-group-divergence problem: the min is the boundary a
  restore can actually rely on), multiply by the uniform chunk-token
  size (`self._log_chunk_tokens`, already used by the LOAD side), and
  report that delta as the token column instead. Moved the log call from
  before the per-group loop to after it, since the "after" value isn't
  known until the loop has run. Added a note with both the new
  cumulative RAM-backed total and (already in scope as
  `num_tokens_after_batch`) the current VRAM-resident total, and called
  the direction a copy, not an eviction, directly in the comment.
- LOAD: kept the existing accurate "GPU had N tok" (before) and added
  "now N+M tok in VRAM" (after) -- exact and free, since it's just the
  existing `num_computed_tokens + num_hit_tokens`.

Before/after:

    KV STORE chatcmpl-... | VRAM -> RAM  |   4 blk /   1664 tok (now 53248 tok backed up in RAM, 55744 tok in VRAM)
    KV LOAD  chatcmpl-... | RAM  -> VRAM |  44 blk /  36608 tok (had 50752 tok, now 87360 tok in VRAM)

Verification: syntax-checked (ast.parse), `verify.sh --no-server` green.
Not yet observed against live traffic -- the delta math (before/after
min next_stored_chunk_idx across groups) is new and should be watched on
the next restart to confirm the numbers look sane (delta tok column
divisible by chunk size, monotonically non-decreasing "now X backed up"
across a session for any given request).
